Area lights: filter the LTC lookup tables in the shader

The LTC LUTs are uploaded as R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT and read through
SAMPLER_LINEAR_CLAMP, but linear filtering of that format is optional
in Vulkan. On a device without it, the validation layer reports
VUID-vkCmdDrawIndexed-magFilter-04553 for every scene draw (the LUTs
are bound in the scene uniform set whether or not an area light is
present), and the filtered result is undefined.

Fetch the four texels and interpolate them in the shader instead, with
a nearest sampler. On a device that does filter the format, renders of
an AreaLight3D scene before and after differ by at most 7/255 in 20 of
1.4M pixels (Mobile) and 1/255 (Forward+).

Converting the LUTs to half floats, which always support linear
filtering, is not an option: low-roughness grazing-angle texels hold
values below the half-float normal range, which Godot's conversion
flushes to zero, so 1/z in the inverse LTC matrix becomes infinite.

Applied by godot/CMakeLists.txt on top of GODOT_GIT_REF, after 0003.

--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/area_lights_inc.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/area_lights_inc.glsl
@@ -322,13 +322,30 @@ void ltc_evaluate(vec3 normal, vec3 eye_vec, mat3 M_inv, vec3 points[4], vec4 te
 	integral = I / (2.0 * M_PI);
 }
 
+// Bilinear lookup done by hand: the LUTs are 32-bit float, and linear filtering
+// of R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT is optional in Vulkan. lut_sampler is only used for
+// the fetches, so a nearest sampler is passed.
+vec4 ltc_lut_bilinear(texture2D lut, sampler lut_sampler, vec2 uv) {
+	const int LTC_LUT_LAST = 63;
+	vec2 pos = uv * vec2(float(LTC_LUT_LAST + 1)) - vec2(0.5);
+	vec2 base = floor(pos);
+	vec2 f = pos - base;
+	ivec2 i0 = clamp(ivec2(base), ivec2(0), ivec2(LTC_LUT_LAST));
+	ivec2 i1 = clamp(ivec2(base) + ivec2(1), ivec2(0), ivec2(LTC_LUT_LAST));
+	vec4 t00 = texelFetch(sampler2D(lut, lut_sampler), i0, 0);
+	vec4 t10 = texelFetch(sampler2D(lut, lut_sampler), ivec2(i1.x, i0.y), 0);
+	vec4 t01 = texelFetch(sampler2D(lut, lut_sampler), ivec2(i0.x, i1.y), 0);
+	vec4 t11 = texelFetch(sampler2D(lut, lut_sampler), i1, 0);
+	return mix(mix(t00, t10, f.x), mix(t01, t11, f.x), f.y);
+}
